    "reading": {
        "body": "Eight open cryptography roles cluster around three employers, with IonQ alone accounting for five of them in Geneva.\n\nThe pattern is concentration, not breadth. IonQ posts five distinct seniority levels, from senior engineer to distinguished leader, all in one city and all dated the same day. ServiceNow posts three platform cryptography roles across two California sites. Cloudflare contributes one. The listings come from a mix of European aggregators and company career boards, which is why a single employer can appear five times without that reflecting the wider market.\n\nFor AI specifically, this data says little directly. Cryptography hiring is adjacent to compute infrastructure, since secure key management and post-quantum migration matter to any large distributed system, but nothing here ties these roles to AI workloads, data centers, or power. IonQ is a quantum computing company, and its Geneva cluster reads as a buildout of one team rather than a sector-wide signal.\n\nWhat the data does not cover is the denominator. Eight postings over roughly a week, drawn from a source list that includes federal, aggregated, and remote boards, cannot establish whether cryptography hiring is rising, falling, or flat. The absence of USAJobs and the remote-only boards from the results is as notable as what appears, and it may reflect the narrow window rather than the market.",
